<article class="env-lemma" id="0G29">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0G29">Lemma <span data-tag="0G29">63.10.1</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a finite type separated morphism of quasi-compact and quasi-separated schemes. Let $\Lambda $ be a ring. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
Let $K_ i \in D^+_{tors}(X_{\acute{e}tale}, \Lambda )$, $i \in I$ be a family of objects. Assume given $a \in \mathbf{Z}$ such that $H^ n(K_ i) = 0$ for $n < a$ and $i \in I$. Then $Rf_!(\bigoplus _ i K_ i) = \bigoplus _ i Rf_!K_ i$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $\Lambda $ is torsion, then the functor $Rf_! : D(X_{\acute{e}tale}, \Lambda ) \to D(Y_{\acute{e}tale}, \Lambda )$ commutes with direct sums. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By construction it suffices to prove this when $f$ is an open immersion and when $f$ is a proper morphism. For any open immersion $j : U \to X$ of schemes, the functor $j_! : D(U_{\acute{e}tale}) \to D(X_{\acute{e}tale})$ is a left adjoint to pullback $j^{-1} : D(X_{\acute{e}tale}) \to D(U_{\acute{e}tale})$ and hence commutes with direct sums, see Cohomology on Sites, Lemma <a href="/tag/08FJ" data-tag="08FJ">21.20.8</a>. In the proper case we have $Rf_! = Rf_*$ and we get the result from Étale Cohomology, Lemma <a href="/tag/0GIW" data-tag="0GIW">59.52.6</a> in the bounded belo case and from Étale Cohomology, Lemma <a href="/tag/0F0D" data-tag="0F0D">59.96.4</a> in the case that our coefficient ring $\Lambda $ is a torsion ring. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>